//github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119#issuecomment-445484964","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119","id":445484964,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NTQ4NDk2NA==","user":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-08T19:47:29Z","updated_at":"2018-12-08T19:48:59Z","body":"ok so after all the fixes improving error messages, we still have (for https://getpsalm.org/r/9b16b5294b) the following error message\r\n\r\n> ERROR: LessSpecificImplementedReturnType - 36:16 - The return type 'Foo' for \r\n AlmostFoo::makeFoo is more specific than the implemented return type for AlmostFooMap::makefoo 'T&Foo'\r\n\r\n`Foo` is actually less specific than `T&Foo` so, as you suggested, it's a problem of return type covariance not working with templates (it works fine for standard interfaces: https://getpsalm.org/r/dd9373aac0)\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/445484964/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2014121150,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjAxNDEyMTE1MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/events/2014121150","actor":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"closed","commit_id":"c6f451a8b72570f35d4f096e449fa845c9c6af84","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/commits/c6f451a8b72570f35d4f096e449fa845c9c6af84","created_at":"2018-12-08T20:17:48Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/445572364","html_url":"https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119#issuecomment-445572364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119","id":445572364,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NTU3MjM2NA==","user":{"login":"aidantwoods","id":3288888,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg4ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3288888?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods","html_url":"https://github.com/aidantwoods","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-09T21:15:18Z","updated_at":"2018-12-09T21:15:18Z","body":"Awesome work, thanks for fixing that! :)\r\n\r\nA couple of minor nits (sorry! 😃):\r\nIt seems that the intersection type prevents Psalm from doing type deduction to properly specify the templated type, and that Psalm then \"upcasts\" to `mixed`: https://getpsalm.org/r/6bbd19a07e\r\n\r\n```\r\nINFO: MixedTypeCoercion - 49:5 - The type 'AlmostFooMap<mixed>' is more general than the declared return type 'AlmostFooMap<FooImplementer>' for bar\r\n\r\nINFO: MixedTypeCoercion - 46:13 - The declared return type 'AlmostFooMap<FooImplementer>' for bar is more specific than the inferred return type 'AlmostFooMap<mixed>'\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think that if Psalm knows the concrete type for any intersection expression involving (any number of) templated types then they should all get assigned to that concrete type\r\n\r\ne.g. with `T`, `U` templated and `Foo` an already known type: if Psalm needs to check that a specified `someClass` is a `T&U&Foo` when instantiating a templated object, then it must check that `someClass` is a `Foo`, and then it can set `T` is a `someClass` and `U` is a `someClass` (it's possible that `T` and `U` could be allowed to be more general than `someClass`, but they cannot be more specific).\r\n\r\nMaybe this is a feature request as I'm not sure this was technically expected to be supported?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI think this shouldn't be allowed: https://getpsalm.org/r/9872014b22, the constructor accepts a closure that returns just `T`, and then assigns it to an instance variable which is a closure that returns `T&Foo`. Then permits an actual usage of a non `Foo` as `T`.\r\n\r\nI can open these as separate issues if you prefer? \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/445572364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"aidantwoods","id":3288888,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg4ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3288888?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods","html_url":"https://github.com/aidantwoods","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/comments/445579486","html_url":"https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119#issuecomment-445579486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1119","id":445579486,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NTU3OTQ4Ng==","user":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-09T22:50:49Z","updated_at":"2018-12-09T22:50:49Z","body":"> Maybe this is a feature request as I'm not sure this was technically expected to be supported?\r\n\r\nYeah, definitely a feature request. I feel like what's really desired is something like this 